Dialogue: 1,0:01:35.33,0:01:38.50,Q1,,0,0,0,,Countless new residents have arrived\Nin the Great Tree Village.
Dialogue: 1,0:01:39.75,0:01:42.46,Q1,,0,0,0,,Such as the enormous minotaurs.
Dialogue: 1,0:01:44.17,0:01:46.92,Q1,,0,0,0,,The half-horse, half-humanoid centaurs.
Dialogue: 1,0:01:47.96,0:01:50.79,Q1,,0,0,0,,The nyunyu daphne wood spirits.
Dialogue: 1,0:01:51.42,0:01:54.42,Q1,,0,0,0,,In order to welcome our 200 new residents,
Dialogue: 1,0:01:55.38,0:01:59.58,Q1,,0,0,0,,we invited representatives from\Neach race to discuss how to proceed.
Dialogue: 1,0:02:00.83,0:02:04.42,Q1,,0,0,0,,Allow me to apologize for not having\Nsuitable homes ready for you.
Dialogue: 1,0:02:04.42,0:02:10.04,Q1,,0,0,0,,I'd hoped to ask for your help\Nin getting your peoples settled here...
Dialogue: 1,0:02:10.63,0:02:12.54,Q1,,0,0,0,,You really don't need to be that deferent.
Dialogue: 1,0:02:12.54,0:02:15.46,Q1,,0,0,0,,Nonsense! In your presence,
Dialogue: 1,0:02:15.46,0:02:18.17,Q1,,0,0,0,,I am little more than a flake of dust\Nfallen in the corner of this room.
Dialogue: 1,0:02:18.17,0:02:19.67,Q1,,0,0,0,,House dust, huh?
Dialogue: 1,0:02:20.29,0:02:22.42,Q1,,0,0,0,,Let's all just relax and-
Dialogue: 1,0:02:24.08,0:02:25.29,Q1,,0,0,0,,A cue card?
Dialogue: 1,0:02:28.79,0:02:30.46,Q1,,0,0,0,,I choose to allow it this time.
Dialogue: 1,0:02:31.00,0:02:32.46,Q1,,0,0,0,,You'd best be grateful.
Dialogue: 1,0:02:32.92,0:02:35.92,Q1,,0,0,0,,Now lift up your head, Gruwald Raby Coll.
Dialogue: 1,0:02:38.08,0:02:41.96,Q1,,0,0,0,,I have high hopes for\Nthe work you will perform.
Dialogue: 1,0:02:43.54,0:02:45.83,Q1,,0,0,0,,Sir! It is my pleasure to serve!
Dialogue: 1,0:02:45.83,0:02:47.08,Q1,,0,0,0,,Thanks.
Dialogue: 1,0:02:47.33,0:02:52.33,Q1,,0,0,0,,We all now live together, so let us\Nput aside formalities and take it easy.
Dialogue: 1,0:02:52.83,0:02:56.58,Q1,,0,0,0,,I have assigned each of your people\Na representative who will look after you.
Dialogue: 1,0:02:57.25,0:02:59.13,Q1,,0,0,0,,Narf will attend to the minotaurs.
Dialogue: 1,0:02:59.13,0:03:01.13,Q1,,0,0,0,,Lattiaci to the centaurs.
Dialogue: 1,0:03:01.13,0:03:02.96,Q1,,0,0,0,,It is my pleasure.
Dialogue: 1,0:03:02.96,0:03:05.46,Q1,,0,0,0,,And for the nyunyu daphne...
Dialogue: 1,0:03:05.88,0:03:09.00,Q1,,0,0,0,,Mamu! At your service.
Dialogue: 1,0:03:10.00,0:03:11.75,Q1,,0,0,0,,We are glad to have you.
Dialogue: 1,0:03:12.00,0:03:14.88,Q1,,0,0,0,,I will do all that I can!
Dialogue: 1,0:03:15.33,0:03:19.75,Q1,,0,0,0,,Mamu moved here from Howling Village\Nalong with Sena and the others.
Dialogue: 1,0:03:20.29,0:03:22.21,Q1,,0,0,0,,Mamu can handle it!
Dialogue: 1,0:03:22.79,0:03:28.71,Q1,,0,0,0,,I tasked her with this after Sena\Nrecommended her for a higher-level position.
Dialogue: 1,0:03:29.88,0:03:33.38,Q1,,0,0,0,,Now, as for where\Neach of your people will live...
Dialogue: 1,0:03:33.63,0:03:38.13,Q1,,0,0,0,,The village we had built was\Nmeant for human-sized beings.
Dialogue: 1,0:03:39.21,0:03:44.04,Q1,,0,0,0,,So instead, we decided to build separate\Nvillages fit for the minotaurs and centaurs.
Dialogue: 1,0:03:44.58,0:03:48.54,Q1,,0,0,0,,The thought was that\Nletting them live separately
Dialogue: 1,0:03:48.54,0:03:51.50,Q1,,0,0,0,,would make it easier to live\Nand work with their people.
Dialogue: 1,0:03:52.63,0:03:55.29,Q1,,0,0,0,,We used the locations\NLea and the others found.
Dialogue: 1,0:03:56.92,0:03:59.54,Q1,,0,0,0,,Building roads and\Nirrigation channels to them.
Dialogue: 1,0:04:00.42,0:04:04.42,Q1,,0,0,0,,There's a lot of forest to clear,\Nso I could use your help.
Dialogue: 1,0:04:04.58,0:04:05.42,Q1,,0,0,0,,Okay!
Dialogue: 1,0:04:05.42,0:04:06.42,Q1,,0,0,0,,All right.
Dialogue: 1,0:04:06.42,0:04:07.25,Q1,,0,0,0,,Ready?
Dialogue: 1,0:04:07.25,0:04:08.08,Q1,,0,0,0,,Go!
Dialogue: 1,0:04:12.67,0:04:13.79,Q1,,0,0,0,,Roar!
Dialogue: 1,0:04:13.79,0:04:15.33,Q1,,0,0,0,,How much should we burn?
Dialogue: 1,0:04:15.33,0:04:16.88,Q1,,0,0,0,,No burning, please!
Dialogue: 1,0:04:17.33,0:04:21.17,Q1,,0,0,0,,Again, I want to build a road\Nin this direction.
Dialogue: 1,0:04:21.67,0:04:22.79,Q1,,0,0,0,,Okay!
Dialogue: 1,0:04:22.92,0:04:23.92,Q1,,0,0,0,,Hup!
Dialogue: 1,0:04:27.29,0:04:28.67,Q1,,0,0,0,,How was that?
Dialogue: 1,0:04:28.67,0:04:30.42,Q1,,0,0,0,,It's the right direction, at least.
Dialogue: 1,0:04:32.46,0:04:33.46,Q1,,0,0,0,,Hrmph.
Dialogue: 1,0:04:36.71,0:04:38.71,Q1,,0,0,0,,I see room for improvement, Lasty.
Dialogue: 1,0:04:39.29,0:04:40.96,Q1,,0,0,0,,I haven't gone all out yet!
Dialogue: 1,0:04:40.96,0:04:42.21,Q1,,0,0,0,,Settle down now!
Dialogue: 1,0:04:42.42,0:04:44.96,Q1,,0,0,0,,We could lose the entire forest at this rate.
Dialogue: 1,0:04:46.54,0:04:49.00,Q1,,0,0,0,,Let's relax, okay? Take it easy. Gently!
Dialogue: 1,0:04:49.00,0:04:51.92,Q1,,0,0,0,,Let's relax, okay? Take it easy. Gently!
Dialogue: 1,0:04:49.00,0:04:51.92,Q4,,0,0,0,,I had them refrain from using their\Nfull power as we progressed.
Dialogue: 1,0:04:51.92,0:04:53.21,Q1,,0,0,0,,What are you dancing for?
Dialogue: 1,0:04:53.21,0:04:55.83,Q1,,0,0,0,,We should continue\Nalongside the river for now.
Dialogue: 1,0:04:56.13,0:04:58.04,Q1,,0,0,0,,These too, if you would!
Dialogue: 1,0:04:58.33,0:04:59.96,Q1,,0,0,0,,Dig! Dig! Dig!
Dialogue: 1,0:05:00.25,0:05:01.96,Q1,,0,0,0,,Pat! Pat! Pat!
Dialogue: 1,0:05:02.25,0:05:05.25,Q1,,0,0,0,,Drop! Drop! Drop!
Dialogue: 1,0:05:05.83,0:05:06.83,Q1,,0,0,0,,Dash!
Dialogue: 1,0:05:09.58,0:05:10.50,Q1,,0,0,0,,Chop!
Dialogue: 1,0:05:15.13,0:05:17.50,Q1,,0,0,0,,This is such a slog. Can't we burn them?
Dialogue: 1,0:05:17.50,0:05:18.50,Q1,,0,0,0,,No.
Dialogue: 1,0:05:21.67,0:05:23.25,Q1,,0,0,0,,I beg your pardon.
Dialogue: 1,0:05:24.50,0:05:26.83,Q1,,0,0,0,,These are for young Alfred.
Dialogue: 1,0:05:28.58,0:05:30.75,Q1,,0,0,0,,The latest from Zabuton.
Dialogue: 1,0:05:31.17,0:05:33.79,Q1,,0,0,0,,They do seem a bit large, however.
Dialogue: 1,0:05:33.79,0:05:36.75,Q1,,0,0,0,,Hasty as ever.
Dialogue: 1,0:05:40.96,0:05:44.75,Q1,,0,0,0,,In the second village, we are\Nconstructing houses for the minotaurs.
Dialogue: 1,0:05:45.29,0:05:50.13,Q1,,0,0,0,,They're quite tall, so we're building\Ntaller one-story homes.
Dialogue: 1,0:05:51.08,0:05:54.00,Q1,,0,0,0,,Yes, not only are the buildings tall,
Dialogue: 1,0:05:54.00,0:05:55.88,Q1,,0,0,0,,but the furniture is large too.
Dialogue: 1,0:05:57.50,0:06:00.04,Q1,,0,0,0,,This is not a table, but a chair.
Dialogue: 1,0:06:00.04,0:06:01.79,Q1,,0,0,0,,That there is the table.
Dialogue: 1,0:06:02.63,0:06:05.29,Q1,,0,0,0,,I feel almost like a child again.
Dialogue: 1,0:06:06.46,0:06:09.00,Q1,,0,0,0,,These are beds?
Dialogue: 1,0:06:09.92,0:06:11.29,Q1,,0,0,0,,They're certainly unique.
Dialogue: 1,0:06:11.29,0:06:12.04,Q1,,0,0,0,,Yes.
Dialogue: 1,0:06:12.04,0:06:14.92,Q1,,0,0,0,,Built so our horns don't hit them.
Dialogue: 1,0:06:16.63,0:06:21.38,Q1,,0,0,0,,Here in our third village,\Nwe have homes for the centaurs.
Dialogue: 1,0:06:22.63,0:06:24.50,Q1,,0,0,0,,As their bodies are built like horses,
Dialogue: 1,0:06:24.50,0:06:27.50,Q1,,0,0,0,,homes built like stables\Napparently suit them best.
Dialogue: 1,0:06:28.04,0:06:30.04,Q1,,0,0,0,,What a wide entrance.
Dialogue: 1,0:06:30.33,0:06:32.29,Q1,,0,0,0,,Will you be adding doors?
Dialogue: 1,0:06:32.29,0:06:37.42,Q1,,0,0,0,,Yes, but my kind have trouble\Nwith ordinary doors.
Dialogue: 1,0:06:39.79,0:06:43.75,Q1,,0,0,0,,So we plan to add a curtain\Ndrawn by rope instead.
Dialogue: 1,0:06:43.75,0:06:45.08,Q1,,0,0,0,,Makes sense.
Dialogue: 1,0:06:45.79,0:06:49.08,Q1,,0,0,0,,They have sliding doors\Nfor rainy days too, apparently.
Dialogue: 1,0:06:50.75,0:06:53.33,Q1,,0,0,0,,Oh, why are you in such a bad mood?
Dialogue: 1,0:06:53.79,0:06:55.50,Q1,,0,0,0,,Allow me.
Dialogue: 1,0:06:56.88,0:06:59.17,Q1,,0,0,0,,Let us begin.
Dialogue: 1,0:06:59.92,0:07:01.08,Q1,,0,0,0,,Peak a boo.
Dialogue: 1,0:07:02.88,0:07:04.54,Q1,,0,0,0,,Peak a boo.
Dialogue: 1,0:07:06.46,0:07:10.38,Q1,,0,0,0,,What did you just do? Show me!
Dialogue: 1,0:07:10.83,0:07:12.25,Q1,,0,0,0,,It's a secret.
Dialogue: 1,0:07:15.63,0:07:17.21,Q1,,0,0,0,,A month went by,
Dialogue: 1,0:07:18.13,0:07:22.21,Q1,,0,0,0,,and everyone's hard work\Nbrought both villages to shape.
Dialogue: 1,0:07:28.46,0:07:32.08,Q1,,0,0,0,,The distance is about this far,\Nmeasured in steps.
Dialogue: 1,0:07:32.08,0:07:34.38,Q1,,0,0,0,,So the third village stands here...
Dialogue: 1,0:07:36.17,0:07:39.00,Q1,,0,0,0,,It's a good thing they're\Nfinished before winter.
Dialogue: 1,0:07:39.00,0:07:40.13,Q1,,0,0,0,,For sure.
Dialogue: 1,0:07:40.67,0:07:43.17,Q1,,0,0,0,,We couldn't leave them\Nout in the winter cold.
Dialogue: 1,0:07:43.38,0:07:44.50,Q1,,0,0,0,,So...
Dialogue: 1,0:07:45.13,0:07:47.63,Q1,,0,0,0,,What will these villages be named?
Dialogue: 1,0:07:47.75,0:07:49.38,Q1,,0,0,0,,Good question.
Dialogue: 1,0:07:49.67,0:07:53.33,Q1,,0,0,0,,Based on location, they could be,\NUpton, Middleton, and Downton...
Dialogue: 1,0:07:53.33,0:07:56.00,Q1,,0,0,0,,But those don't really sound right...
Dialogue: 1,0:07:56.00,0:08:00.25,Q1,,0,0,0,,Maybe just Village One,\NVillage Two, and Village Three.
Dialogue: 1,0:08:00.54,0:08:02.67,Q1,,0,0,0,,These will be temporary,\Nso if anyone has better ideas-
Dialogue: 1,0:08:02.67,0:08:05.17,Q1,,0,0,0,,Let's avoid any changes, shall we?
Dialogue: 1,0:08:05.17,0:08:09.54,Q1,,0,0,0,,Surely you see how hard it is to rewrite\Nevery document we've made?
Dialogue: 1,0:08:09.54,0:08:10.54,Q1,,0,0,0,,Right...
Dialogue: 1,0:08:10.92,0:08:14.38,Q1,,0,0,0,,We can leave Village One\Nunassigned for now,
Dialogue: 1,0:08:14.38,0:08:16.79,Q1,,0,0,0,,but Gordon should be mayor of Village Two.
Dialogue: 1,0:08:17.04,0:08:20.63,Q1,,0,0,0,,And Gruwald mayor of Village Three, yes?
Dialogue: 1,0:08:20.63,0:08:21.96,Q1,,0,0,0,,I guess so.
Dialogue: 1,0:08:21.96,0:08:26.08,Q1,,0,0,0,,But if we name them\Nall mayors like our own...
Dialogue: 1,0:08:26.08,0:08:32.17,Q1,,0,0,0,,Yes, it might be best to create\Na clearer hierarchy with your title.
Dialogue: 1,0:08:32.54,0:08:34.29,Q1,,0,0,0,,Like High Mayor.
Dialogue: 1,0:08:34.29,0:08:35.79,Q1,,0,0,0,,Or Great Mayor.
Dialogue: 1,0:08:35.79,0:08:37.33,Q1,,0,0,0,,Or King Mayor.
Dialogue: 1,0:08:37.33,0:08:39.83,Q1,,0,0,0,,Let's not go that far.
Dialogue: 1,0:08:40.50,0:08:41.83,Q1,,0,0,0,,If I may...
Dialogue: 1,0:08:42.17,0:08:45.08,Q1,,0,0,0,,When will a village be built for my people?
Dialogue: 1,0:08:45.08,0:08:47.17,Q1,,0,0,0,,Ah, sorry.
Dialogue: 1,0:08:47.17,0:08:49.75,Q1,,0,0,0,,We decided against building\Na nyunyu daphne village.
Dialogue: 1,0:08:51.13,0:08:52.54,Q1,,0,0,0,,Is that so...?
Dialogue: 1,0:08:53.08,0:08:55.83,Q1,,0,0,0,,Then our dream of finding\Na home to set our roots
Dialogue: 1,0:08:55.83,0:08:57.42,Q1,,0,0,0,,remains no more than just that.
Dialogue: 1,0:08:57.42,0:08:59.13,Q1,,0,0,0,,Hang on now!
Dialogue: 1,0:08:59.46,0:09:03.83,Q1,,0,0,0,,I have a favor to ask of your people\Nin each of our villages.
Dialogue: 1,0:09:04.63,0:09:10.83,Q1,,0,0,0,,Since the nyunyu daphne\Nare more suited to staying put,
Dialogue: 1,0:09:11.29,0:09:13.29,Q1,,0,0,0,,our plan was to place them\Nat important locations
Dialogue: 1,0:09:13.29,0:09:17.17,Q1,,0,0,0,,and task them with standing watch\Nand relaying information.
Dialogue: 1,0:09:18.04,0:09:23.46,Q1,,0,0,0,,Their kind are able to communicate\Nthrough what seems like telepathy.
Dialogue: 1,0:09:23.63,0:09:24.58,Q1,,0,0,0,,Peaceful.
Dialogue: 1,0:09:24.71,0:09:25.50,Q1,,0,0,0,,Peaceful.
Dialogue: 1,0:09:25.63,0:09:26.63,Q1,,0,0,0,,Peaceful.
Dialogue: 1,0:09:27.21,0:09:29.42,Q1,,0,0,0,,They made perfect messengers.
Dialogue: 1,0:09:29.63,0:09:30.46,Q1,,0,0,0,,Mild.
Dialogue: 1,0:09:30.58,0:09:31.38,Q1,,0,0,0,,Mild.
Dialogue: 1,0:09:31.50,0:09:32.75,Q1,,0,0,0,,Mild?
Dialogue: 1,0:09:33.13,0:09:36.83,Q1,,0,0,0,,Why not ask that they watch over\Nthe uninhabited Village One as well?
Dialogue: 1,0:09:36.83,0:09:38.29,Q1,,0,0,0,,Good thinking!
Dialogue: 1,0:09:38.54,0:09:39.88,Q1,,0,0,0,,Very well!
Dialogue: 1,0:09:40.13,0:09:44.96,Q1,,0,0,0,,It would be unbearable to have it\Nwaste away after all the work put into it.
Dialogue: 1,0:09:45.25,0:09:49.13,Q1,,0,0,0,,We also had them act as lighting\Nin the evenings.
Dialogue: 1,0:09:50.75,0:09:54.38,Q1,,0,0,0,,Now that each race has\Nsettled into their homes,
Dialogue: 1,0:09:54.38,0:09:59.38,Q1,,0,0,0,,I'd like to assign jobs to the residents\Nof villages One and Two, but...
Dialogue: 1,0:10:01.83,0:10:03.21,Q1,,0,0,0,,Hrngh...
Dialogue: 1,0:10:06.17,0:10:07.17,Q1,,0,0,0,,Mayor...
Dialogue: 1,0:10:08.17,0:10:10.04,Q1,,0,0,0,,We have a bit of a problem.
Dialogue: 1,0:10:10.04,0:10:11.96,Q1,,0,0,0,,As do we.
Dialogue: 1,0:10:11.96,0:10:13.25,Q1,,0,0,0,,What sort?
Dialogue: 1,0:10:13.42,0:10:18.63,Q1,,0,0,0,,Apparently, the minotaurs and centaurs\Nweren't suited to hunting in the forest.
Dialogue: 1,0:10:20.50,0:10:23.63,Q1,,0,0,0,,They look plenty strong to me.
Dialogue: 1,0:10:23.92,0:10:26.71,Q1,,0,0,0,,The minotaurs are a tranquil people.
Dialogue: 1,0:10:26.71,0:10:29.13,Q1,,0,0,0,,Some of them are capable in battle,
Dialogue: 1,0:10:29.13,0:10:31.79,Q1,,0,0,0,,but that does not leave them fit for hunting.
Dialogue: 1,0:10:31.92,0:10:37.71,Q1,,0,0,0,,Most of the centaurs are refugees\Nhardly able to fend for themselves.
Dialogue: 1,0:10:38.29,0:10:40.79,Q1,,0,0,0,,I never realized hunting was so difficult
Dialogue: 1,0:10:40.79,0:10:42.92,Q1,,0,0,0,,because the inferno wolves\Nhandled it for us.
Dialogue: 1,0:10:42.92,0:10:46.58,Q1,,0,0,0,,Those wolves have unimaginable strength.
Dialogue: 1,0:10:46.92,0:10:53.75,Q1,,0,0,0,,We should keep the people out of the woods\Nand place more defenders in both villages.
Dialogue: 1,0:10:53.75,0:10:55.21,Q1,,0,0,0,,Good thinking.
Dialogue: 1,0:10:55.75,0:10:58.38,Q1,,0,0,0,,Let's talk with Kuro and Zabuton.
Dialogue: 1,0:10:59.08,0:11:01.75,Q1,,0,0,0,,Do the nyunyu daphne need guards?
Dialogue: 1,0:11:01.75,0:11:04.21,Q1,,0,0,0,,They seem good enough at avoiding combat.
Dialogue: 1,0:11:04.21,0:11:07.33,Q1,,0,0,0,,Well, actually, you know...
Dialogue: 1,0:11:07.50,0:11:08.92,Q1,,0,0,0,,We can do it!
Dialogue: 1,0:11:08.92,0:11:11.08,Q1,,0,0,0,,It seems they're quite strong.
Dialogue: 1,0:11:11.08,0:11:15.38,Q1,,0,0,0,,But they mostly fight via ambush,\Nso they can't hunt large numbers.
Dialogue: 1,0:11:15.83,0:11:17.83,Q1,,0,0,0,,How do they even fight?
Dialogue: 1,0:11:21.29,0:11:24.83,Q1,,0,0,0,,We decided to leave hunting\Nto Kuro and the rest.
Dialogue: 1,0:11:25.25,0:11:28.13,Q1,,0,0,0,,And we set about\Ntilling fields in each village.
Dialogue: 1,0:11:28.38,0:11:34.79,Q1,,0,0,0,,The idea was to make them self-sufficient,\Neven without hunting. But...
Dialogue: 1,0:11:35.63,0:11:38.13,Q1,,0,0,0,,Nothing seems to be taking root.
Dialogue: 1,0:11:39.29,0:11:40.88,Q1,,0,0,0,,Why not?
Dialogue: 1,0:11:41.54,0:11:45.54,Q1,,0,0,0,,Do you always plant\Nthese seeds in this season?
Dialogue: 1,0:11:45.54,0:11:47.58,Q1,,0,0,0,,The seeds? Uhh...
Dialogue: 1,0:11:47.58,0:11:50.38,Q1,,0,0,0,,When did we plant them again?
Dialogue: 1,0:11:50.38,0:11:51.38,Q1,,0,0,0,,Dunno.
Dialogue: 1,0:11:51.38,0:11:52.46,Q1,,0,0,0,,Umm...
Dialogue: 1,0:11:53.04,0:11:58.63,Q1,,0,0,0,,There was a reason we were unsure,\Ndespite raising crops all these years.
Dialogue: 1,0:11:59.00,0:12:04.67,Q1,,0,0,0,,The only reason I was able to raise crops\Nand live in the middle of the forest
Dialogue: 1,0:12:04.67,0:12:08.67,Q1,,0,0,0,,was because I had the power of\Nthe almighty farming tool.
Dialogue: 1,0:12:09.25,0:12:11.96,Q1,,0,0,0,,Its divine powers made soil fertile,
Dialogue: 1,0:12:11.96,0:12:14.88,Q1,,0,0,0,,let me plant any seed I imagined,
Dialogue: 1,0:12:14.88,0:12:17.67,Q1,,0,0,0,,and made the crops grow faster.
Dialogue: 1,0:12:18.00,0:12:21.50,Q1,,0,0,0,,Our ability to harvest\Ndespite the season or weather
Dialogue: 1,0:12:21.50,0:12:24.83,Q1,,0,0,0,,is the main reason we were\Nable to grow to such a size.
Dialogue: 1,0:12:25.29,0:12:28.96,Q1,,0,0,0,,Unfortunately, I am the\Nonly one able to use it.
Dialogue: 1,0:12:28.96,0:12:31.58,Q1,,0,0,0,,It is all I can do to prepare our own fields.
Dialogue: 1,0:12:31.92,0:12:33.92,Q1,,0,0,0,,They're just too big!
Dialogue: 1,0:12:34.29,0:12:37.04,Q1,,0,0,0,,So the new villages are to handle their fields
Dialogue: 1,0:12:37.04,0:12:39.79,Q1,,0,0,0,,without the use of the almighty farming tool.
Dialogue: 1,0:12:40.29,0:12:42.58,Q1,,0,0,0,,This is harder than I thought.
Dialogue: 1,0:12:42.58,0:12:44.75,Q1,,0,0,0,,We'll have to keep trying.
Dialogue: 1,0:12:44.75,0:12:46.04,Q1,,0,0,0,,In that case...
Dialogue: 1,0:12:46.38,0:12:51.83,Q1,,0,0,0,,By laying down straw to keep the soil\Nfrom getting cold, we may have more luck.
Dialogue: 1,0:12:52.13,0:12:56.83,Q1,,0,0,0,,With winter on approach,\Nit might be best to plant wheat.
Dialogue: 1,0:12:56.83,0:12:58.33,Q1,,0,0,0,,You know your stuff.
Dialogue: 1,0:12:58.33,0:12:59.83,Q1,,0,0,0,,Hardly.
Dialogue: 1,0:12:59.83,0:13:03.42,Q1,,0,0,0,,I merely helped with farm work\Non occasion in my last village.
Dialogue: 1,0:13:03.42,0:13:05.33,Q1,,0,0,0,,You have experience, then!
Dialogue: 1,0:13:05.33,0:13:10.33,Q1,,0,0,0,,We continued preparing the fields\Nwith guidance from our farming senpai.
Dialogue: 1,0:13:10.50,0:13:13.21,Q1,,0,0,0,,The wheat we plant now\Nwill sit through the winter
Dialogue: 1,0:13:13.21,0:13:15.88,Q1,,0,0,0,,and be ready for harvest before summer.
Dialogue: 1,0:13:17.25,0:13:20.88,Q1,,0,0,0,,Half a year's wait, huh?\NI guess that's the norm.
Dialogue: 1,0:13:21.04,0:13:24.08,Q1,,0,0,0,,We've grown too accustomed to\Nthe Great Tree Village's fields.
Dialogue: 1,0:13:24.08,0:13:25.33,Q1,,0,0,0,,Seems like.
Dialogue: 1,0:13:25.88,0:13:30.83,Q1,,0,0,0,,It's probably not normal for pineapples\Nto grow in such snowy climates.
Dialogue: 1,0:13:31.50,0:13:35.79,Q1,,0,0,0,,All the more reason to be grateful\Nto the god of agriculture!
Dialogue: 1,0:13:36.21,0:13:37.75,Q1,,0,0,0,,What might these be?
Dialogue: 1,0:13:37.75,0:13:41.58,Q1,,0,0,0,,Statues of the gods of creation\Nand agriculture.
Dialogue: 1,0:13:41.83,0:13:45.13,Q1,,0,0,0,,I was thinking of building a shrine\Nand housing them there.
Dialogue: 1,0:13:45.13,0:13:47.46,Q1,,0,0,0,,Oh, please do.
Dialogue: 1,0:13:49.46,0:13:51.79,Q1,,0,0,0,,These are fantastic sculptures.
Dialogue: 1,0:13:51.79,0:13:56.00,Q1,,0,0,0,,The one with the stick is the God of Creation,\Nbut who is the other?
Dialogue: 1,0:13:56.00,0:13:57.96,Q1,,0,0,0,,The God of Agriculture, apparently.
Dialogue: 1,0:13:58.96,0:14:01.08,Q1,,0,0,0,,That's an interesting take on them.
Dialogue: 1,0:14:01.71,0:14:05.13,Q1,,0,0,0,,Guess different lands have\Ndifferent interpretations.
Dialogue: 1,0:14:07.38,0:14:10.38,Q1,,0,0,0,,Farming Life in Another World 2!
Dialogue: 1,0:14:12.58,0:14:16.04,Q1,,0,0,0,,While the minotaurs handled agriculture...
Dialogue: 1,0:14:16.25,0:14:17.46,Q1,,0,0,0,,Keep up!
Dialogue: 1,0:14:17.75,0:14:18.63,Q1,,0,0,0,,Yes, ma'am!
Dialogue: 1,0:14:18.63,0:14:23.00,Q1,,0,0,0,,...the centaurs used their abilities\Nto develop a new line of work.
Dialogue: 1,0:14:23.88,0:14:28.29,Q1,,0,0,0,,Their Centaur Delivery service began\Nshipping goods between villages.
Dialogue: 1,0:14:28.88,0:14:31.25,Q1,,0,0,0,,They were unfit for hunting,
Dialogue: 1,0:14:31.25,0:14:33.88,Q1,,0,0,0,,but more than able to outrun\Nany monsters.
Dialogue: 1,0:14:34.38,0:14:40.00,Q1,,0,0,0,,The adult centaurs were each tasked\Nwith regular deliveries.
Dialogue: 1,0:14:44.88,0:14:46.88,Q1,,0,0,0,,New route record!
Dialogue: 1,0:14:49.58,0:14:50.75,Q1,,0,0,0,,Oww...
Dialogue: 1,0:14:50.75,0:14:52.42,Q1,,0,0,0,,Perhaps that was too fast.
Dialogue: 1,0:14:52.42,0:14:55.38,Q1,,0,0,0,,I just hope they put safety first.
Dialogue: 1,0:14:57.04,0:15:00.08,Q1,,0,0,0,,Mayor, a moment, if I may.
Dialogue: 1,0:15:00.08,0:15:01.29,Q1,,0,0,0,,What is it?
Dialogue: 1,0:15:01.29,0:15:05.25,Q1,,0,0,0,,I noticed you have a horse on your farm here.
Dialogue: 1,0:15:05.25,0:15:07.29,Q1,,0,0,0,,We do, yeah.
Dialogue: 1,0:15:07.30,0:15:12.29,Q1,,0,0,0,,Our merchant friend brought us one\Nalong with goats and chickens.
Dialogue: 1,0:15:12.83,0:15:16.13,Q1,,0,0,0,,I've always wanted to ride a horse, you know.
Dialogue: 1,0:15:16.29,0:15:17.75,Q1,,0,0,0,,Unfortunately...
Dialogue: 1,0:15:17.75,0:15:19.04,Q1,,0,0,0,,Hey!
Dialogue: 1,0:15:19.29,0:15:21.79,Q1,,0,0,0,,Look! I've got a carrot!
Dialogue: 1,0:15:22.42,0:15:25.00,Q1,,0,0,0,,...it doesn't listen to a word I say.
Dialogue: 1,0:15:25.63,0:15:31.29,Q1,,0,0,0,,If you can communicate with horses,\Ncan you ask it to give me a ride?
Dialogue: 1,0:15:31.54,0:15:36.04,Q1,,0,0,0,,I'm sorry, I do not speak horse.
Dialogue: 1,0:15:36.04,0:15:41.17,Q1,,0,0,0,,However, if that horse is not\Nyour trusty steed...
Dialogue: 1,0:15:44.83,0:15:46.58,Q1,,0,0,0,,Hup!
Dialogue: 1,0:15:47.46,0:15:49.08,Q1,,0,0,0,,Okay. All set.
Dialogue: 1,0:15:49.33,0:15:51.17,Q1,,0,0,0,,Let us begin.
Dialogue: 1,0:15:55.08,0:15:58.08,Q1,,0,0,0,,Wow, we're up so high!
Dialogue: 1,0:15:58.08,0:15:59.92,Q1,,0,0,0,,Grab hold of my shoulders if you wish.
Dialogue: 1,0:16:01.00,0:16:02.83,Q1,,0,0,0,,Please hold on tight.
Dialogue: 1,0:16:05.08,0:16:07.25,Q1,,0,0,0,,Whoa! What a bumpy ride.
Dialogue: 1,0:16:07.46,0:16:09.38,Q1,,0,0,0,,We'll now pick up the pace.
Dialogue: 1,0:16:14.33,0:16:15.33,Q1,,0,0,0,,Sorry.
Dialogue: 1,0:16:15.33,0:16:16.54,Q1,,0,0,0,,Not at all.
Dialogue: 1,0:16:17.33,0:16:21.88,Q1,,0,0,0,,How does it feel taking your first ride?
Dialogue: 1,0:16:22.63,0:16:24.13,Q1,,0,0,0,,It's great!
Dialogue: 1,0:16:26.75,0:16:28.00,Q1,,0,0,0,,Hmm?
Dialogue: 1,0:16:28.50,0:16:30.58,Q1,,0,0,0,,What's with you all of a sudden?
Dialogue: 1,0:16:31.25,0:16:34.25,Q1,,0,0,0,,You know how to let someone ride now, is it?
Dialogue: 1,0:16:34.54,0:16:36.75,Q1,,0,0,0,,Okay, giddy up!
Dialogue: 1,0:16:37.21,0:16:39.92,Q1,,0,0,0,,Good! Keep that up.
Dialogue: 1,0:16:42.42,0:16:44.00,Q1,,0,0,0,,How can this be?!
Dialogue: 1,0:16:44.21,0:16:45.71,Q1,,0,0,0,,Good work.
Dialogue: 1,0:16:46.63,0:16:47.92,Q1,,0,0,0,,There, there.
Dialogue: 1,0:16:49.67,0:16:50.75,Q1,,0,0,0,,What?!
Dialogue: 1,0:16:54.58,0:16:56.58,Q1,,0,0,0,,In a good mood, huh?
Dialogue: 1,0:16:56.58,0:16:58.42,Q1,,0,0,0,,How dare you...
Dialogue: 1,0:17:01.96,0:17:04.17,Q1,,0,0,0,,Good morning, Mayor!
Dialogue: 1,0:17:04.17,0:17:05.79,Q1,,0,0,0,,Lovely day, isn't it?
Dialogue: 1,0:17:07.29,0:17:09.08,Q1,,0,0,0,,What's going on here?
Dialogue: 1,0:17:09.08,0:17:11.71,Q1,,0,0,0,,You are headed off, yes?\NPlease, ride on me!
Dialogue: 1,0:17:11.71,0:17:17.54,Q1,,0,0,0,,It's too dangerous to ride\Nthis strange, wild beast!
Dialogue: 1,0:17:17.54,0:17:18.92,Q1,,0,0,0,,That's my horse, though.
Dialogue: 1,0:17:18.92,0:17:20.13,Q1,,0,0,0,,See? It's dangerous!
Dialogue: 1,0:17:20.13,0:17:21.54,Q1,,0,0,0,,It's not even wild.
Dialogue: 1,0:17:21.54,0:17:24.25,Q1,,0,0,0,,Let's settle down and be friends, okay?
Dialogue: 1,0:17:24.25,0:17:26.08,Q1,,0,0,0,,Friends!
Dialogue: 1,0:17:24.25,0:17:26.08,Q4,,0,0,0,,What are you dancing for?
Dialogue: 1,0:17:26.08,0:17:26.54,Q1,,0,0,0,,Friends!
Dialogue: 1,0:17:26.54,0:17:28.17,Q1,,0,0,0,,I will hold you to your word.
Dialogue: 1,0:17:29.25,0:17:32.25,Q1,,0,0,0,,I didn't want them\Nwaiting for me every morning,
Dialogue: 1,0:17:32.25,0:17:34.54,Q1,,0,0,0,,so I promised to ride each every other day.
Dialogue: 1,0:17:40.67,0:17:41.79,Q1,,0,0,0,,So, umm!
Dialogue: 1,0:17:41.79,0:17:44.58,Q1,,0,0,0,,Is there anything I can do for you?
Dialogue: 1,0:17:47.38,0:17:49.96,Q1,,0,0,0,,Anything you need?
Dialogue: 1,0:17:49.96,0:17:51.63,Q1,,0,0,0,,Or don't understand?
Dialogue: 1,0:17:51.63,0:17:54.29,Q1,,0,0,0,,You can ask for anything!
Dialogue: 1,0:17:55.38,0:17:56.46,Q1,,0,0,0,,The sky.
Dialogue: 1,0:17:56.46,0:17:57.63,Q1,,0,0,0,,Yes?!
Dialogue: 1,0:17:58.92,0:18:00.13,Q1,,0,0,0,,Is blue.
Dialogue: 1,0:18:00.13,0:18:02.63,Q1,,0,0,0,,Yes! What lovely weather!
Dialogue: 1,0:18:08.21,0:18:13.75,Q1,,0,0,0,,The roots of the crops grow deeper\Nthan imagined, so it's best to till deep.
Dialogue: 1,0:18:13.75,0:18:15.63,Q1,,0,0,0,,Understood, Gordon-senpai!
Dialogue: 1,0:18:15.63,0:18:17.79,Q1,,0,0,0,,All seems to be well.
Dialogue: 1,0:18:17.79,0:18:19.00,Q1,,0,0,0,,Yup.
Dialogue: 1,0:18:19.33,0:18:24.08,Q1,,0,0,0,,At first, I was worried about\Nthe huge influx all at once.
Dialogue: 1,0:18:24.42,0:18:26.17,Q1,,0,0,0,,How are you feeling?
Dialogue: 1,0:18:26.17,0:18:27.83,Q1,,0,0,0,,Well enough, thank you.
Dialogue: 1,0:18:27.83,0:18:32.42,Q1,,0,0,0,,I hope each village can\Neventually support itself.
Dialogue: 1,0:18:32.67,0:18:35.42,Q1,,0,0,0,,For now, they all rely on you.
Dialogue: 1,0:18:35.42,0:18:37.54,Q1,,0,0,0,,It's nice to be useful.
Dialogue: 1,0:18:37.54,0:18:41.83,Q1,,0,0,0,,But I'd like them to be able to\Nresolve some things on their own.
Dialogue: 1,0:18:42.42,0:18:47.21,Q1,,0,0,0,,Relying too much on the convenience\Nof the almighty farming tool
Dialogue: 1,0:18:47.21,0:18:49.42,Q1,,0,0,0,,would leave me worried for the future.
Dialogue: 1,0:18:49.83,0:18:53.83,Q1,,0,0,0,,I'm healthy and well\Nthanks to divine powers, but...
Dialogue: 1,0:18:56.71,0:19:01.67,Q1,,0,0,0,,Never know when a cold\Nmight knock me out, right?
Dialogue: 1,0:19:03.17,0:19:05.42,Q1,,0,0,0,,We can deal with that when it happens.
Dialogue: 1,0:19:07.04,0:19:13.04,Q1,,0,0,0,,Worry all you want, you won't be\Nretiring carefree soon anyway.
Dialogue: 1,0:19:13.71,0:19:15.71,Q1,,0,0,0,,So perhaps you ought just relax.
Dialogue: 1,0:19:17.17,0:19:18.46,Q1,,0,0,0,,You think?
Dialogue: 1,0:19:18.46,0:19:19.75,Q1,,0,0,0,,I do!
Dialogue: 1,0:19:20.46,0:19:22.08,Q1,,0,0,0,,I guess so.
Dialogue: 1,0:19:25.63,0:19:27.21,Q1,,0,0,0,,What's wrong?
Dialogue: 1,0:19:28.38,0:19:29.92,Q1,,0,0,0,,Oh, I can smell the answer.
Dialogue: 1,0:19:29.92,0:19:31.54,Q1,,0,0,0,,You handed him over on purpose, didn't you?
Dialogue: 1,0:19:31.54,0:19:33.88,Q1,,0,0,0,,Best get that diaper changed!
Dialogue: 1,0:19:35.17,0:19:39.17,Q1,,0,0,0,,While reflecting an unusual amount\Non my own future,
Dialogue: 1,0:19:39.17,0:19:42.96,Q1,,0,0,0,,I remembered another\Nimportant problem we faced.
Dialogue: 1,0:19:43.58,0:19:47.58,Q1,,0,0,0,,The Great Tree Village is filled with women.
Dialogue: 1,0:19:48.13,0:19:50.63,Q1,,0,0,0,,Beyond filled. Overflowing!
Dialogue: 1,0:19:52.42,0:19:55.33,Q1,,0,0,0,,By comparison,\Nthere are hardly any men.
Dialogue: 1,0:19:55.33,0:19:58.13,Q1,,0,0,0,,This has me worried\Nabout our future.
Dialogue: 1,0:19:58.13,0:20:01.13,Q1,,0,0,0,,I've asked for new male inhabitants,
Dialogue: 1,0:20:01.13,0:20:03.25,Q1,,0,0,0,,but have had no luck.
Dialogue: 1,0:20:03.71,0:20:06.79,Q1,,0,0,0,,But now we have a great\Nnumber of newcomers!
Dialogue: 1,0:20:06.79,0:20:09.21,Q1,,0,0,0,,This should solve those worries!
Dialogue: 1,0:20:09.54,0:20:11.88,Q1,,0,0,0,,Men?
Dialogue: 1,0:20:12.46,0:20:16.71,Q1,,0,0,0,,Of our 72, 28 are male.
Dialogue: 1,0:20:16.71,0:20:18.83,Q1,,0,0,0,,Is that right?
Dialogue: 1,0:20:18.83,0:20:21.63,Q1,,0,0,0,,Do we need soldiers?
Dialogue: 1,0:20:21.83,0:20:25.63,Q1,,0,0,0,,Are we to be sent off to battle?
Dialogue: 1,0:20:25.63,0:20:27.63,Q1,,0,0,0,,Nope! Nothing like that.
Dialogue: 1,0:20:27.63,0:20:30.17,Q1,,0,0,0,,So it's like this, see?
Dialogue: 1,0:20:30.17,0:20:32.46,Q1,,0,0,0,,Which means that and that!
Dialogue: 1,0:20:32.46,0:20:33.92,Q1,,0,0,0,,I see...
Dialogue: 1,0:20:34.13,0:20:39.92,Q1,,0,0,0,,It is custom for us minotaurs\Nto marry other minotaurs.
Dialogue: 1,0:20:39.92,0:20:43.21,Q1,,0,0,0,,Due to our size, if nothing else.
Dialogue: 1,0:20:43.21,0:20:45.42,Q1,,0,0,0,,Hadn't thought of that.
Dialogue: 1,0:20:45.88,0:20:52.17,Q1,,0,0,0,,For better or worse, the minotaurs were\Nto be left to marry among their own.
Dialogue: 1,0:20:52.63,0:20:54.71,Q1,,0,0,0,,Which left the centaurs.
Dialogue: 1,0:20:54.71,0:20:57.38,Q1,,0,0,0,,It felt wrong to bring\Nthis question to the women,
Dialogue: 1,0:20:57.38,0:20:59.54,Q1,,0,0,0,,...but it had to be done\Nfor the sake of our future!
Dialogue: 1,0:20:59.92,0:21:02.04,Q1,,0,0,0,,Our men?
Dialogue: 1,0:21:02.42,0:21:08.13,Q1,,0,0,0,,Thirty of our own are male,\Nbut all are but boys.
Dialogue: 1,0:21:08.13,0:21:10.79,Q1,,0,0,0,,The adults are off at war.
Dialogue: 1,0:21:10.79,0:21:12.08,Q1,,0,0,0,,I see...
Dialogue: 1,0:21:12.08,0:21:14.58,Q1,,0,0,0,,So you have boys, if not men yet.
Dialogue: 1,0:21:15.33,0:21:19.83,Q1,,0,0,0,,This might be hard to answer,\Nbut I must stress that it is important.
Dialogue: 1,0:21:21.08,0:21:23.21,Q1,,0,0,0,,It's in regards to centaur marriages.
Dialogue: 1,0:21:23.21,0:21:25.08,Q1,,0,0,0,,I am single!
Dialogue: 1,0:21:25.08,0:21:26.96,Q1,,0,0,0,,That's fine and all, but...
Dialogue: 1,0:21:27.21,0:21:31.58,Q1,,0,0,0,,Do centaurs ever marry other races?
Dialogue: 1,0:21:31.58,0:21:33.88,Q1,,0,0,0,,Not ordinarily.
Dialogue: 1,0:21:33.88,0:21:36.46,Q1,,0,0,0,,This is a difficult hurdle, I guess.
Dialogue: 1,0:21:36.88,0:21:41.88,Q1,,0,0,0,,It may prove difficult for centaurs\Nto pair with other races.
Dialogue: 1,0:21:42.21,0:21:47.58,Q1,,0,0,0,,However, if you demand one of our women\Nas price for our home here...
Dialogue: 1,0:21:47.58,0:21:49.21,Q1,,0,0,0,,No, it's not like that.
Dialogue: 1,0:21:49.58,0:21:51.25,Q1,,0,0,0,,I ask that you take me!
Dialogue: 1,0:21:51.25,0:21:52.96,Q1,,0,0,0,,I am prepared to serve!
Dialogue: 1,0:21:52.96,0:21:53.88,Q1,,0,0,0,,What?!
Dialogue: 1,0:21:53.88,0:21:56.67,Q1,,0,0,0,,Relax, I'm not asking for anything like that.
Dialogue: 1,0:21:56.67,0:21:57.58,Q1,,0,0,0,,Why not?
Dialogue: 1,0:21:57.58,0:21:58.46,Q1,,0,0,0,,Why what?!
Dialogue: 1,0:21:58.46,0:22:02.17,Q1,,0,0,0,,Do men not enjoy overpowering strong women?
Dialogue: 1,0:22:02.17,0:22:03.25,Q1,,0,0,0,,Who told you that?
Dialogue: 1,0:22:03.67,0:22:05.71,Q1,,0,0,0,,Just relax, okay? Relax...
